}}'''Mount Quidamortem''' ({{IPAc-en|ˈ|k|w|ɪ|d|ər|m|ɒr|t|ə|m}} {{respell|KWID|ər|mort|əm}}{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1318995542270246914|date=21 October 2020|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/100330|archivedate=28 July 2022|quote=KWID-er-mort-em.}}) is a mountain in the [[Kebos Lowlands]]. Underneath Mount Quidamortem are the [[Chambers of Xeric]], which serves as the staging ground for raids, as well as the [[Quidamortem Cave]], which is visited during the [[Tale of the Righteous]] [[quest]].

==Transportation==
[[File:Path to Raids.png|thumb|250px|Paths to Mount Quidamortem.]]
Players who haven't unlocked fairy rings will have to travel to the mountain on foot. Players can walk south-west past [[Shayziens' Wall]] and run westward until they reach the mountain. A form of [[poison]] protection should be taken as there are aggressive [[Lizardmen]] of all types patrolling the east side of the mountain. Just before the mountain base, there should be some [[big frog]]s and [[goblin]]s wandering the area. At the base of the mountain will be some [[mountain troll]] settlements and a large group of [[rock crab]]s.

When players reach the summit, find the [[Mountain Guide]] and speak with him to unlock a travel point between the mountain, the Wall, and south of Mount Quidamortem. This will save a considerable amount of time should players enter from Shayzien. Players who have unlocked fairy rings can also use {{fairycode|BLS}} south of Quidamortem, and then utilise the Mountain Guide to travel to the mountain.

It can also be quickly accessed via the [[Lovakengj Minecart Network]], and then running north.

Once players receive an [[ancient tablet]] as a reward from the [[Chambers of Xeric]], they are able to use it on [[Xeric's talisman]] to unlock the ability to instantly teleport to the mountain with the "Xeric's Honour" option.

==History==
{{LoreSources|Mount karuulm diary|Tekton's journal|The Great Expedition|Ektheme|Gnosi|Phileas Rimor|Imerominia|the1=yes|dialogue6=yes|dialogue7=yes|dialogue4=yes|dialogue5=yes}}

Mount Quidamortem was likely first discovered by the [[dragonkin]] [[Karuulm]] prior to the founding of [[Great Kourend]]. He was drawn to it by [[Lizard (Quidamortem)|a species of lizard]] that showed potential for experimentation. These experiments led to the creation of the [[Great Olm]].

On 1,740 - 36 (''the 1,740th day of the 36th decade''), [[King Shayzien VII]] ordered an expedition west to the [[Kebos Lowlands]], seeking to explore and expand the territory of [[Great Kourend]]. The expedition team never returned, and it was assumed that all members perished in the field, leading the King to declare that the expedition was a failure.

However, an old journal written by Shayzien VII in the following decade suggests that the expedition deemed the native lizards of the region were suitable for a certain experiment: the creation of the [[lizardmen]]. For this purpose, a cave was created in the side of the mountain, with an altar resembling the [[Dark Altar]] constructed inside, allowing the actual Dark Altar's power to reach the Kebos Lowlands.

Shortly after the death of Shayzien VII in the [[Battle of the Concourse]], [[Xeric]] made his appearance and took over [[Great Kourend]]. However, in 332 - 47, he was forced into exile, and travelled to Mount Quidamortem with his most loyal followers. Here, he explored the caverns beneath the mountain, and created the [[Chambers of Xeric]] in order to harness the power of the crystals to empower himself and those loyal to him. It was not until over 1,000 years later that the [[Kebos Lowlands]] was opened back up, after [[Shayzien]] soldiers repelled most of the [[lizardmen]] to the caverns below their [[Lizardman Settlement|settlement]].

==Locations==

=== Structures ===
The main feature is Tekton's temple, a large stone dome at the peak of the mountain which hosts a [[Xerician Statue|Xerician statue]] in the centre. Just to the north of this temple is the entrance to the [[Chambers of Xeric]].

To the east of the temple are three cloth-covered buildings; the two nearest the mountain hold the [[Mount Quidamortem bank]] chest and its associated [[poll booth]], and the far building contains sleeping bag for the Varrock Museum expedition crew.

=== Skill training spots ===
Apart from the personalities and local fauna, the lake south of Historian Duffy has [[barbarian fishing]] spots. These spots are significantly closer to a [[Mount Quidamortem bank|bank]] than the spots at [[Baxtorian Falls]], which is particularly useful when using the [[fish barrel]]. There is also a [[Fire|permanent fire]] in the troll camp, as well as [[Dead tree|dead trees]] scattered throughout the mountain.

=== Troll camp ===
South of the mountain peak is a troll camp, featuring multiple spots with mountain trolls in a [[multicombat area]]. This makes the [[dwarf multicannon]] effective on troll [[Slayer task]]s. The best cannon spot can be found across the bridge.

